{
  "coreName": "RPCS3",
  "systemId": "PS3",
  "systemNames": {
    "PS3": "PlayStation 3"
  },
  "extensions": {
    ".elf": "PS3",
    ".self": "PS3",
    ".bin": "PS3",
    ".iso": "PS3",
    ".zip": "PS3",
    ".pkg": "PS3"
  },
  "media": [
    {
      "id": "disc",
      "label": "PlayStation 3 disc",
      "_comment": "For the frontend's media maker (Tools > Reproducible Media Maker), when it packs a folder with PS3_DISC.SFB at its root as an ISO. RPCS3 reads a region table from the first sector of a disc image - a big-endian count, then each region's first and last sector - and refuses a count below 1 as \"not a PS3 ISO\". A decrypted folder dump is one region, not encrypted, ending on the image's last sector, and that is what this writes. It is a FORMAT: everybody who packs the same dump must get the same file, so these values never change.",
      "format": "iso9660",
      "when": {
        "rootFile": "PS3_DISC.SFB"
      },
      "systemArea": [
        {
          "at": 0,
          "u32be": 1
        },
        {
          "at": 12,
          "u32be": "lastSector"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "author": "the RPCS3 Team",
  "url": "https://github.com/RPCS3/rpcs3",
  "romFile": "game",
  "deterministic": true,
  "memoryLayoutMiB": [
    1024,
    16,
    64,
    256,
    40960
  ],
  "_memoryLayoutMiB_note": "sbrk, sealed, invisible, plain, mmap. The PS3's flat 4 GiB guest view (aligned to 4 GiB, so the arena spends 8 to place it and gives half back), the 10 GiB execution table, the 2 GiB JIT arena, the LLVM recompiler's regions and the emulator's large allocations come out of the mmap arena; a precompile walks a hundred modules through it. Everything is a reservation: pages are committed as the machine touches them, on Windows too (miniBox spec v2), so the size costs address space and the sandbox's page bookkeeping, not memory.",
  "video": {
    "greenzoneSurvivesReload": true,
    "_comment_greenzone": "TRUE: a project's greenzone this core drew on a GPU may be loaded by a later session (docs/gpu-bridge.md in Chimera, 'Keeping the greenzone across sessions'). Measured 2026-09-16: a PopCap title, 1000 frames, a 100 MB greenzone loaded in a fresh process; frame 999 identical (0 of 921,600 pixels differ; the frame is 72.6% black, so the match rests on its 252,811 lit pixels), a control frame differing by 99.82%. Until 2026-10-18 this was RPCS3's name on a list in Chimera.",
    "_comment": "buffer CAPACITY: the PS3 outputs up to 1920x1080; the live size comes from GetVideoWidth/Height per frame and follows the display buffer the machine flips. 720p is the console's usual mode. 60 Hz exactly: the vblank thread schedules in whole microseconds of machine time.",
    "width": 1920,
    "height": 1080,
    "virtualWidth": 1280,
    "virtualHeight": 720,
    "vsyncNumerator": 60,
    "vsyncDenominator": 1,
    "getBgra": "GetVideoBgra",
    "gpuStatesSurviveTheContext": true,
    "_comment_gpuStates": "The renderer keeps the context id its GL objects came from (the bridge's GL_OP_CONTEXT_ID) and builds them again when the calls start landing on another one - which is what loading a savestate in a later session does. So a state this core makes can be opened again."
  },
  "audio": {
    "_comment": "cellAudio's 48 kHz stereo mix, drained by machine time: 800 frames per vblank, silence when the machine mixed less.",
    "samplesPerFrame": 16384,
    "channels": 2,
    "get": "GetAudio"
  },
  "lag": {
    "inputWasRead": "InputWasRead"
  },
